DATA NOTICES

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code in this repository. The data the
pipeline fetches and the small, allow-listed caches it commits come from public
sources under their own terms. Polaris is a research-planning tool, not medical
advice. The committed dataset keeps only identifiers, labels, dates, status
fields and one-sentence quotes; abstracts, author lists, contact details and
eligibility text are never committed (see the README, "How the dataset is
made").

Human Phenotype Ontology (HPO) - hpo.jax.org; Gargano et al., NAR 2024.
  Used for symptom terms and similarity. Polaris annotations are marked as such
  and are not part of HPO.
Orphadata: free access data from Orphanet (c) INSERM 1999, orphadata.com,
  version <date of the committed download>. Used for gene-disease links and
  the three direction labels in the slice.
Monarch Initiative - monarchinitiative.org (semsim API); Disorder Mechanisms KB,
  github.com/monarch-initiative/dismech (BSD-3, pre-alpha). Used for phenotype
  similarity and as a cross-check of mechanism claims.
ClinicalTrials.gov (U.S. National Library of Medicine) - data retrieved through
  the v2 API. Listing does not imply NLM endorsement or our evaluation of a study.
PubMed / NCBI E-utilities (NLM) - citations and one-sentence excerpts only;
  abstracts are (c) their publishers and are not redistributed here.
PubTator3 / LitVar2 (NCBI) - variant normalisation; Wei et al., NAR 2024.
Gene2Phenotype (EMBL-EBI) - inferred mechanism labels, cited by entry ID.
HGNC, MONDO, UniProt, ClinGen - identifiers and cross-checks (CC0 / CC BY 4.0).
Open Targets Platform (CC0 1.0), including ChEMBL (EMBL-EBI) - drug and
  mechanism data for the researcher screen (release and retrieval date in
  pipeline/screen/cache/drug_pool.json); no ChEMBL document records. The
  "approved medicines" total counts ChEMBL max-phase-4 molecule ids (ChEMBL
  molecule endpoint, CC BY-SA 3.0, ids only) whose Open Targets stage is
  APPROVAL, collapsed to ChEMBL parent molecules (salts count once; esters are
  separate molecules); their preferred and trade names are kept (lower-cased,
  drug_pool.json -> approved_names) only so the post-check can reject any
  model sentence that names a medicine other than the card's own.
IMSR / JAX / MMRRC / RIKEN BRC - model stock identifiers only; availability must
  be confirmed with the repository.

Patient-organisation websites are linked, never copied. scn8a.net asks not to
be mined and is linked only. Release dates and retrieval dates are recorded in
the dataset itself (graph.json -> meta).
